# GitHub's "Cite this repository" button and Zenodo's release archive both read this.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this template, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "project-templates"
# The concept DOI, which always resolves to the newest release.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23701980"
abstract: >-
  A Copier template for provenance-first data pipelines, where every row of a dataset
  built from public sources says which download it came from, plus Python, TypeScript,
  Rust, Go and Docker projects. Every project gets supply-chain-hardened CI, and public
  ones get community files and OpenSSF Scorecard; the web-app kind adds legal pages and an
  accessibility statement.
authors:
  - given-names: "Simon"
    family-names: "van Lierde"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6953-909X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/simonvanlierde/project-templates"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - copier
  - project template
  - research software
  - provenance
  - data pipeline
  - supply-chain security
  - web app
